forfex is an independent clean-room implementation of the
architecture described in:

  Qu, Huang, Yin, Zhan, Liu, Yin, Cousins, Johnson, Wang, Shah,
  Altman, Zhou, Wang, Cong. "CRISPR-GPT for agentic automation of
  gene-editing experiments." Nat Biomed Eng 2026;10(2):245-258.
  doi:10.1038/s41551-025-01463-z

It is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from the
authors' implementation. No code, prompts, or data from
cong-lab/crispr-gpt-pub were used. See docs/clean-room.md.

forfex orchestrates third-party bioinformatics tools as separate
processes. Those tools carry their own licences and are not
redistributed with forfex. See docs/third-party.md.
